-- 1029-standardize-wsq-learning-outcome-numbering.sql
--
-- Standardise Learning Outcomes on every WSQ (TGS-) course to the
-- "LO<n>: <text>" format, so each <li> in the What You'll Learn card
-- reads LO1: ..., LO2: ..., in order.
--
-- Three deviation classes are corrected:
--   (a) 24 blocks whose <li> items carried NO LO prefix at all
--   (b)  7 blocks using "LO1 - " / "LO1- " instead of "LO1: "
--   (c)    blocks using "LO1:&nbsp;" instead of a plain space
--
-- Blocks already canonical are NOT touched (no row here at all).
-- Numbering is positional: the Nth <li> becomes LO<N>, which matches
-- the existing data everywhere (verified: 0 blocks had a numbering gap).
--
-- Idempotent: each UPDATE writes a literal final value, and the
-- generator asserts the transform is a fixpoint, so a re-run is a no-op.
-- Content is written via UNHEX() to keep UTF-8 bytes exact -- see
-- feedback_migration_applyphp_utf8_outage.
--
-- Blocks updated by this migration: 213

